# OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Chrome extension type) from Google Cloud Console.
# Same Google Cloud project as your Firebase app. Rebuild after changing.
#
# Local Google sign-in:
# 1. npm run build → Load unpacked from dist/ → copy Extension ID
# 2. GCP → Credentials → OAuth client → Application type: Chrome extension → paste ID
# 3. Set VITE_CHROME_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID below and rebuild
# 4. GCP → Credentials → OAuth client → Application type: Web application
#    Authorized redirect URI (no trailing slash):
#    https://YOUR_EXTENSION_ID.chromiumapp.org
# 5. Set VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID (needed for Arc/Brave; Chrome can use either)
# 6. Firebase → Authentication → enable Google provider
# 7. Firebase → Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains: chrome-extension://YOUR_ID
# 8. Deploy firestore.rules (backups/{uid} read/write for request.auth.uid == uid)
VITE_CHROME_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
